{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/57","id":4687071616,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF18JgA","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/57","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/57.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/57.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/57","number":57,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"30003354: reviewed conformal parametrization counterexamples at every integer endpoint","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Result and scope\n\nThis draft contains a complete candidate negative answer to the specified conformal-metric parametrization question for every finite integer r>=0, on both the plane and the sphere.\n\nThe counterexample sequences consist of smooth complete strictly positive-curvature metrics converging in C^r, while their uniquely normalized conformal diffeomorphisms fail to converge in C^(r+1). The r=1 endpoint includes an exact nonlinear curvature-preserving correction; curvature continuity in C^1 is not assumed.\n\nThe proof concerns this particular parametrization. It does not rule out other product homeomorphisms, and it does not contradict the known Hölder or C-infinity statements. The source's 2016 erratum and exact derivative shift are documented.\n\n## Independent validation\n\n- Frozen CANDIDATE.md SHA-256: 7f358fb1aaa73dc3cfd06c798c10f6afed65ee430b622b84b90f0554dd440e62\n- Separate adversarial review: PASS_COMPLETE_COUNTEREXAMPLE; no mandatory corrections\n- All 90 submitted symbolic assertions reproduce byte-for-byte\n- All 136 independent exact assertions pass\n- Complete review, source checks and reproducible scripts included\n\nReproduce the submitted checks with `python3 unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003354/verify.py` and the independent checks with the script in `independent_review/` (Python3 and SymPy).\n\nThis is an AI-reviewed, unrefereed candidate result. Historical priority is unconfirmed and no new-discovery claim is made. One substantive attempt,1/5. No source PDFs, external publication, release or merge is included.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T07:01:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T07:03:33Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c729e3a154f53c42950e1e05f5bc137bcf8c116b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/57/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/57/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/57/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/4ecc453d6f9ec2e64cdb2d4b41c018fffbe85b29","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-30003354","ref":"dot/math-30003354","sha":"4ecc453d6f9ec2e64cdb2d4b41c018fffbe85b29","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNz